Multiple stages operate simultaneously.

CPUs do the same thing.

Typical pipeline stages:

Fetch

↓

Decode

↓

Execute

↓

Memory

↓

Write Back

While one instruction executes, another is decoding, and another is being fetched.

This overlap greatly increases throughput.

Why Pipelines Matter
Suppose:

Instruction 1

Instruction 2

Instruction 3

Without a pipeline:

Fetch

Decode

Execute

Fetch

Decode

Execute

With a pipeline:

Cycle1

Fetch I1

Cycle2

Decode I1

Fetch I2

Cycle3

