Why Happens-Before Exists
Before understanding happens-before, remember the problem.

A normal Java program:

int value = 0;

Two threads:

Thread A:

value = 100;

Thread B:

System.out.println(value);

The developer expects:

Thread A writes 100
        |
        |
        v
Thread B reads 100

But the JVM and CPU are allowed to do:

Thread A:

write value=100

↓

store buffer

↓

cache


Thread B:

read old cached value

