What Is volatile?
A volatile variable is a variable whose reads and writes have special guarantees defined by the Java Memory Model.

Example:

private volatile boolean running = true;

When one thread writes:

running = false;

another thread reading:

while (running) {

}

is guaranteed to observe the change.

